{"lines":[{"w":0.67467554728190104,"y":0.094431699264816649,"x":0.08655308532715153,"h":0.03685364873154362,"c":1,"t":"Sample answers for Writing tasks"},{"t":"TEST 1, WRITING TASK 1","y":0.16080886338370859,"w":0.34907768249511723,"c":1,"x":0.086520970137592593,"h":0.023772735115866972},{"c":1,"t":"SAMPLE ANSWER","x":0.08670520438309344,"y":0.19905660364063071,"h":0.014606187328602527,"w":0.19845856984456384},{"y":0.23679245299336038,"w":0.67822733561197923,"t":"This is an answer written by a candidate who achieved a Band 6.5 score.","h":0.017610062893081757,"c":1,"x":0.086705214497399458},{"w":0.79768783569335944,"t":"The diagrams illustrate the average proportions of three types of nutrients in typical meals, which","c":1,"y":0.26598837232670358,"x":0.08477843268353695,"h":0.018917288270386412},{"w":0.80924855550130226,"h":0.020348837990430857,"c":1,"y":0.28633720890847925,"x":0.084778419663109894,"t":"can be unhealthy if consumed too much. The three types include sodium, saturated fats and added"},{"y":0.3056331468879121,"t":"sugar. The data is taken from the United States of America.","h":0.023048506442855832,"c":1,"x":0.084640479954237735,"w":0.49347447713216142},{"c":1,"w":0.8034682210286459,"h":0.020451221825941612,"t":"The first chart shows the average percentages of sodium. Dinner contains the most sodium (43%).","x":0.084778413473605194,"y":0.3371069180968076},{"w":0.79978586832682286,"h":0.022564898796801347,"x":0.08662132671812571,"c":1,"y":0.35682868323392869,"t":"Breakfast and snacks include an equal proportion of sodium consumed, with each of them adding"},{"x":0.084778414051714324,"y":0.37924528245183464,"w":0.78034683227539059,"h":0.020464020255226645,"c":1,"t":"up 14% of sodium. Through eating lunch, 29% sodium is consumed. The second chart shows the"},{"t":"percentages of saturated fat in meals. By eating dinner, 31% saturated fat is consumed. Lunch","w":0.76685933430989572,"h":0.020449393650270986,"y":0.40251572301636185,"c":1,"x":0.086705207523495365},{"x":0.084778411405190088,"h":0.01890448984110138,"t":"contributes to a consumption of 26% saturated fat, followed by snacks with 21% and breakfast with","y":0.42295597503516025,"w":0.80154144287109375,"c":1},{"t":"16%. The last chart illustrates the proportions of added sugar. Snacks contain the highest amount","w":0.79961466471354159,"y":0.44465408800522166,"x":0.084778409358065313,"c":1,"h":0.019008702452077753},{"h":0.020348837990430857,"x":0.084778423765170224,"c":1,"y":0.46656976704885045,"t":"of added sugar (42%). Dinner includes 23% A typical dinner includes 23% added sugar, while lunch","w":0.81310211181640624},{"c":1,"y":0.48581809459160752,"t":"contains 19% and breakfast includes 16%.","x":0.084668429450544092,"h":0.018606492408416497,"w":0.335532709757487},{"h":0.020489615914206838,"w":0.81310211181640635,"t":"All in all, the diagrams show that every typical meal consumed in the USA contains a percentage of","x":0.086705206008284297,"y":0.51598837169878586,"c":1},{"h":0.018950197231844546,"c":1,"y":0.53773584903906269,"w":0.53371866861979167,"x":0.086705212802128534,"t":"at least 14% of nutrients that can be unhealthy if eaten too much."},{"c":1,"h":0.017007536858132832,"x":0.08660519502217881,"y":0.57459998253833433,"t":"Here is the examiner's comment:","w":0.30659154256184895},{"x":0.13288065644314126,"h":0.01933950028329523,"c":1,"y":0.61090946081929787,"t":"The candidate has accurately reported the data for each chart and has presented","w":0.74774230957031251},{"y":0.63081395375027216,"h":0.017441859935064752,"x":0.13294796783208218,"w":0.68208094278971354,"t":"a summary of the information, but could achieve a higher score by making","c":1},{"h":0.017610062893081757,"w":0.71676300048828123,"c":1,"t":"comparisons across the charts, e.g. breakfast contains the lowest amounts of","y":0.64968553450431976,"x":0.13102119718916033},{"w":0.72254333496093748,"h":0.017441859935064752,"t":"sodium, saturated fats and added sugar. The information is logically organised","x":0.13102120348174576,"c":1,"y":0.66715116304906619},{"c":1,"x":0.13294798896658885,"y":0.68604651189011046,"w":0.74951828002929688,"t":"and there is a clear progression throughout the script. The main points are clearly","h":0.017441859935064752},{"t":"signalled [The first chart | The second chart | All in all] and there are examples of","y":0.70494186075594678,"w":0.74373794555664063,"h":0.016127321855077148,"c":1,"x":0.13294798281035716},{"y":0.72383720956479392,"w":0.73410405476888019,"t":"other cohesive devices [each of them]. The range of vocabulary is varied [data |","c":1,"x":0.13294797252995655,"h":0.017441859935064752},{"w":0.72254333496093759,"h":0.016072472986185304,"t":"contains | an equal proportion of | consumed | consumption | illustrates]. Minor","c":1,"x":0.13294798562797855,"y":0.74273255842950825},{"x":0.13294798488532783,"t":"errors do not cause misunderstanding [adding up 14% of sodium]. There is a mix","h":0.017610062893081757,"w":0.74566472371419268,"y":0.76006289295225837,"c":1},{"y":0.77893081732543112,"w":0.74951828002929688,"h":0.019182389937106858,"c":1,"t":"of simple and complex sentence structures, using active, passive and modal verb","x":0.13294798911033864},{"w":0.76878611246744799,"c":1,"y":0.79651162816741261,"t":"forms and there is also subordination through the use of participles [Through eating","h":0.017441859935064641,"x":0.13102120183290217},{"w":0.77071289062500004,"h":0.016039564024727282,"c":1,"t":"lunch | By eating dinner | followed by]. More variety in grammatical structures would","x":0.13294798634465868,"y":0.81540697703188436},{"h":0.014558651762188624,"w":0.29865125020345051,"t":"perhaps achieve a higher score.","x":0.132947977889674,"y":0.83575581366924767,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.86897880603607636,"t":"127","h":0.014534883079288852,"y":0.95058139552430909,"w":0.034682079950968392}],"w":2400,"h":3179}